	This might have been talked many times over in which case no flames
please...;)

	As I understand, in NH dungeon may collapse for some reason.  It hasn't
happened to me, but then again, I've never managed to get VERY deep in NH, say
beyond the 20th level.  Further, the collapsing dungeon has been caused in
certain cases by a bug, right? (I'm not sure.)

	Anyway, what I thought of was this.

	Collapsing dungeon might be an interesting feature if implemented
with a bit of thought.  For example, the walls of the corridors, roofs of the
rooms and walls might be of varying firmness or solidity.  There could be a 
command like 'examine walls' or something which you could use to find out if 
the walls of the corridors or rooms were strong or about to collapse on your
neck from like a battle in the room.  Naturally, most of the rooms would just
be ordinary solid no-problem rooms and corridors.  But some of them might
be a bit more dangerous...

	# Examine walls

	  The walls seem to be decayed, just about to crumble on you.

	  The Forest Centaur hits.

	  You are thrown against the wall by the Forest Centaur's hit!

	  The decayed walls crumble!  You are covered under stones and 
	  sand.  (causing the loss of hit points, damage to armor, or even
	  death)

	
	Spells of great power might cause the dungeon or roof to collapse,
	so you'd have to use magic with a bit more concideration.  Before
	casting a spell it would be a good idea to check the condition
	of the dungeon walls.  Same with the wands, of course.

	This could also serve as a means of escaping monsters.  Causing a
	minor collapse just behind you (involving a risk of getting 	
	buried or hurt yourself) could block the way from monsters
	after you or at least slow them down.  

	The pick axe would prove to be useful if going down a corridor which
	has partly collapsed - you could re-open the corridor with it.

	A friend just suggestet that the automatically figuring the state
	of the dungeon walls upon entering a room or a corridor might also
	be an intelligence based 'throw'.  Intelligent characters would
	notice the state of dungeons almost immediately - a bit less
	bright characters might have to check it out more closely with
	the command 'examine walls' for example.  Examinetion could also
	be based on your int.  Luck would also affect.

	Drat, gotta go.  

	This might be an interesting and fun feature.  I'd like to
	hear your comments and suggestions!


